For the necessity of b), one is immediately reduced to the case where $V$ is reduced to a point, where this reduces to the \deleted{``conjectural consequence'' of the preliminary \unsure{conjecture-question}.}

\margin{\figure{\begin{tikzpicture}\draw (0,0)--(0,-4.3);\end{tikzpicture}}}
\uline{Conjectural consequence} Let $\Gamma'\subset\operatorname{Im}(E_U\longrightarrow\Gamma_{\mathbb{Q}})$ be an open subgroup, corresponding to a field $k$ finite over $\mathbb{Q}$, consider a $k$-point of $U$, whence a lift $\Gamma'\longrightarrow E_U$, so that $\Gamma'$ acts on $\Pi_U$. This being so, one has
\[
\Pi_U^{\Gamma'^\circ}=\{1\}.
\]

We shall study later the relations between this ``conjectural'' \inserted{consequence}, and the preceding one (opposite in appearance !) concerning the $E_K$.

The fundamental conjecture on models implies the fundamental conjecture on fields, provided one takes care, in the latter, to restrict oneself to homomorphisms compatible with the model filtrations,
\margin{and it \unsure{is better} to confine oneself to the equivalence of a) and b) -- the conditions c) on centralizers \unsure{may} not pass well to the \uline{limit}.}

More generally, taking \inserted{(\unsure{complete} for $U$)} schemes, \deleted{of dimension} which are $\varprojlim$ of \unsure{anabelian|anabelian} \deleted{schemes} \inserted{elementary models}, with affine transition morphisms \inserted{open immersions}
